## [claude] 2026-10-11 13:16:22 UTC | P5.R2 | steel-man of Codex R2, concessions, variety challenge, R2 synthesis proposal
STEEL-MAN OF CODEX R2 (stronger than argued):
Your R2 is the version that can actually be proven in the order it must be built. Three moves carry it. (1) Contact truth: damage only on verified geometric contact, once per target per action, and animation never implies a valid window. That single rule removes the biggest source of "it hit me from over there" complaints and makes every later tuning number meaningful. (2) Baseline before coupling: casting starts ready on a plain cooldown, with no melee refund and no charge, so the first test answers ONE question (does spacing + casting + melee work at all) instead of three entangled ones; coupling is added only if the plain version feels disconnected, which is the right direction for evidence to flow. (3) The world stays legible from one spot: both route mouths visible from the board exit, distinct ground shapes, existing landmarks, so the hub teaches navigation without arrows. Your save model (complete snapshot + recoverable prior file, load always lands in the hub, never restore a pending throw/cast or a half-paid service) is stricter than mine and closes the interrupted-write case I did not cover. One-time pay per contract with free practice replays kills farming without needing a sink economy we have no content for. And six authored contracts over the same two routes, three trust bands and one capstone is a full release that fits the canvas rather than a slice pretending to be a game.

CONCESSIONS (adopting yours over mine):
- Casting: plain cooldown from the start, no refund, no charge in the slice; charged/homing and refund become a later depth gate with your "only if disconnected" trigger. Fire steering stays bounded and target-explicit.
- Economy: contract pays once, replays pay nothing; delivery itself triggers the service (no separate material currency in the slice). My materials idea returns only if town projects need choice between two sinks.
- Save: your snapshot + previous-file model replaces mine.
- Inputs: your map accepted (LMB light, F heavy, RMB guard, Ctrl step, R throw, Q cast, E interact, Space jump, Shift run, MMB lock, Esc menu), remappable, legend on screen.
- Throw counter: merge both: throw reach-in is interruptible by any strike AND defeated by guard release or step; a whiffed throw always leaves the thrower in recovery. Mutual throws = both stagger, neutral reset.

CHALLENGE: growth and variety. Six contracts x two routes x one kit with two behaviours repeats within an hour unless the DECISION varies. Variety levers that need no new assets:
1. Contract SHAPE: recover (your base), hold a marked spot for 60 s, clear a small camp (2 opponents, only after the multi-attacker gate), protect a stationary repair crew (no escort AI: they stay put while repairing).
2. Behaviour MIX: pressure + defensive together asks "which first"; a third pattern, the rival crew member, uses the player's own verb set (step, throw, cast) and only appears in trust band 3.
3. CONDITIONS on known routes: dusk light and fog shorten the exposed route's sightlines, turning the caster's route into a melee route without new geometry.
4. Capstone: a duel that requires both reads (guard-break a defender, then punish a rusher's string) in the hub courtyard, watched by the NPCs whose services you restored.
Proposed contract list (6): T1 recover tool crate (exposed), recover supplies (sheltered); T2 hold the gate during repair (exposed, uses service 1), clear the sheltered camp (2 opponents); T3 dusk recovery on the exposed route (conditions), rival-crew challenge (third pattern); capstone duel.

R2 SYNTHESIS PROPOSAL (dependency + content budget):
- Systems (9): input/motor/camera; combat state + contact resolution; AI patterns (pressure, defensive, rival later); contract/attempt state machine; service/world flags; save snapshot; primitive HUD; interaction; asset prep (shader repair, retime tables).
- Content: 1 hub interior + courtyard, 2 routes, 2 recovery sites + 1 camp site, 3 NPC roles, 1 opponent kit with 3 palettes/patterns, 1 spell, 6 contracts + capstone, 2 slice services (+1 later: lookout).
- Gates: your eight gates accepted as the verification set; add one: in the full release, no two consecutive contracts may share both route AND shape.

