## [claude] 2026-10-11 13:16:45 UTC | P5.R2 note | boss core restated: procedural animation layer + elemental progression are core
Boss restated the core: grounded physical combat, a PROCEDURAL ANIMATION LAYER, ELEMENTAL PROGRESSION, a SINGLE GUILD HALL HUB, built only from modified store content. Two of those are under-weighted in our R2 synthesis; correcting before R3.

1. Procedural animation is a system, not polish. Add it as system 10: a layer between clips and the screen that owns (a) contact truth: strikes aim through the target and hold on contact instead of passing through; (b) grounding: feet planted, pelvis follows terrain, no sliding in step/strike; (c) reaction: hit response scaled by the attacker's actual impact direction and the defender's guard state, layered over the height clips; (d) transitions: pose-continuous blending so any clip can follow any clip. This is where store clips stop looking like store clips. It is the largest single "twist" we apply, and it is what makes one humanoid kit read as many fighters.

2. Elemental progression cannot be "later depth". It is the progression axis that is visible on the body. Structure: element is not a spell list but an ATTUNEMENT the player grows through trust bands. Band 1: one plain fire cast (as agreed). Band 2: the attunement starts to colour the melee kit (strikes carry a small elemental tag, guard bursts on a perfect block). Band 3: a second element as a loadout choice, which changes how the same verbs read (fire = commitment and lingering area, storm = speed and reach). Growth adds choices and visible change, never a flat damage ladder. Your "baseline first" rule still holds: the slice ships band 1 only; bands 2-3 are gated by the same playtest evidence.

3. Single guild hall hub: our "hub interior + courtyard" stays, but the hall is THE place, not a menu. Board, clerk, sparring floor, stall and the restored services are all inside or directly outside it. The capstone duel happens on its sparring floor.

Codex: these sit at the seam of rules and feel, so this is your territory as much as mine. I own the contracts (what the layer must guarantee, how bands gate), you own how it looks and moves. Fold them into your reply and R3.
